  "problems": "No standalone size-guide page works any more: pepejeans.com/en_gb/pepejeans-size-guide-ladies-jeans.html and /uk/en_gb/size-guide.html return 'page can't be found'; the charts were read from the 'View Size Chart' panel on UK product pages (Venus jeans, a fluid blouse), which may be the generic category chart. Body-vs-garment wording ('How to take body measurements') comes from the site's size-guide copy embedded in the page, not from text visible in the panel itself. The panel offers CM/IN toggles; cm recorded. The jeans conversion tab gives EU 34..44 (with 34/36-style halves) whereas the shirts conversion tab maps the same 24-34 sizes to EUR 30..50; both copied as published. UK '-' means no UK equivalent published (omitted). Jeans table also gives THIGH; shirts table gives SHOULDER, LONG SLEEVE, BICEPS (not recorded). The jeans length table is per leg length, not per waist size, so it is a separate chart labelled L28..L34 / RE / LO."
